{"tag":"HN1Z","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"lemma-1","file":"","label":"mylemma","number":"3.1","section":"sec-3","order":4,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{mylemma}\nIf $\\varphi$ is a locally-balanced $2$-partition with an open neighborhood of a graph $G$, then for every $v \\in V(G)$ with $d_G(v)=2$, $\\varphi(u_1) \\neq \\varphi(u_2)$, where $vu_1,vu_2 \\in E(G) ~(u_1\\neq u_2)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mylemma"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":191,"to":193},"hash":"sha256:6bbc54f0967537138ca5375f182c621c6f26967f899df3b1129eaf58b9d0e72a","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"tag":"S7O3","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"theorem-3","file":"","label":"mytheorem7","number":"3.2","section":"sec-3","order":5,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{mytheorem7}\nA $(2,2k+1)$-biregular bipartite graph $G$ ($k\\in \\mathbb{N}$) with bipartition $(X,Y)$ has a locally-balanced $2$-partition with an open neighborhood if and only if it has no cycle of length $2 \\pmod{4}$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mytheorem7"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":206,"to":208},"hash":"sha256:eb9c9290a3aad247e10df0bfced09b2c8842979ad6db3c349ce5e8e306226710","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
