{"tag":"J7P3","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"lemma-3","file":"","label":"mylemma3","number":"4.1","section":"sec-4","order":11,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{mylemma3}\nIf $\\varphi$ is a locally-balanced $2$-partition with a closed neighborhood of graph $G=(V,E)$, then for every $v \\in V(G)$ with $d_G(v)=1$, $\\varphi(u) \\neq \\varphi(v),\\;$ where $uv \\in E(G)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mylemma3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":437,"to":439},"hash":"sha256:faf96e5db66c457106b31c1aaec33ce070007173ed40aa5204c57c3be30626d5","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"tag":"2VJG","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"lemma-4","file":"","label":"mylemma4","number":"4.2","section":"sec-4","order":12,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{mylemma4}\n\\textit{If a graph $F_2$ has $\\varphi$ locally-balanced $2$-partition with a closed neighborhood, then $\\varphi(v_1) = \\varphi(v_2) = \\varphi(v_5) = \\varphi(v_6)$ and $\\varphi(v_3) = \\varphi(v_4) = 1 - \\varphi(v_1)$. }","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mylemma4"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":463,"to":465},"hash":"sha256:8126260d2404da08ba65391c2d80dbe1c8da935ce6e9b4699f79aea1268bcc57","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-12","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"tag":"9CIZ","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"lemma-5","file":"","label":"mylemma5","number":"4.3","section":"sec-4","order":13,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{mylemma5}\nIf a graph $G=(F_3^i \\left[p^i_1,p^i_2,p^i_3,p^i_4 \\right] \\cup H)_{E'}$ has $\\varphi$ locally-balanced 2-partition with a closed neighborhood, then $\\varphi(p^i_1) = \\varphi(p^i_2) = \\varphi(p^i_3) = \\varphi(p^i_4)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mylemma5"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":498,"to":500},"hash":"sha256:0cfb52aa537243d330e84fe53ed40a3ec658369f7cee4b11eb78a462414d9ff5","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-13","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"tag":"KM8G","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2401.15490","version":"1","local":"lemma-6","file":"","label":"mylemma6","number":"4.4","section":"sec-4","order":14,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{mylemma6}\nIf $\\varphi$ is a $2$-partition of a graph $G=(F_3^i \\left[p^i_1,p^i_2,p^i_3,p^i_4 \\right] \\cup H)_{E'}$, $\\varphi(p^i_j)=\\varphi(v^i_l)$ $(1 \\leq j \\leq 4, \\; 1 \\leq l \\leq 22)$ and $\\varphi(u^i_j) = 1 - \\varphi(p^i_1)$ $(1 \\leq j \\leq 20)$, then $\\#[v^i_j]_\\varphi = 0$ $(1 \\leq j \\leq 22)$, $\\#[u^i_j]_\\varphi = 0$ $(1 \\leq j \\leq 20)$ and $\\#[p^i_j]_\\varphi = \\sum_{w \\in \\{a\\;:\\; ap^i_j\\in E'\\}}\\varphi^*(w)$ $(1 \\leq j \\leq 4)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","labels":["mylemma6"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"main.tex","from":599,"to":601},"hash":"sha256:b430cc0b9ed587fa91d364040b9fc75353133f0a0c60ef783d07a7059b6708b1","minhash":"","census":"2401.15490v1#env-14","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
